title The check wall earns its keep -- the selector map refused by a seated hermeticity assert, withdrawn
prompt Keaton pasted both check-mode refusals: the supervisor's line-503 assert holds /var/select out of the jail plan by name.
think The refusal sits in a family I should have read before editing: no Apple Git, no host GPG, no Apple developer selector -- the jail deliberately excludes mutable host state so the toolchain closure is exactly the pinned homebrew set. The EPERM noise is that design's accepted cost, and my map contradicted a seated decision rather than filling a gap.
think The withdrawal is one commit removing the one --map argument; the hook's speaking refusal stands as the repair that matters -- the next jailed failure prints its inner error, and the surgical fix follows evidence instead of conjecture.
obs Three walls worked in sequence: the check mode I put in the pastes caught the edit before any lap, the seated assert named its reason in its own message, and the withdrawal cost one minute. This is what leading with check buys.
obs The lesson for my own habit, written plainly: before editing a guarded surface, grep its guards for the path being touched -- the supervisor asserts what its plan must and must not contain, and those asserts are the design's memory.
file tools/l/chatgpt-mind.rish the map argument withdrawn; the hermeticity assert untouched
file session-logs/date/20260831/20260831-114656_the-check-wall-earns-its-keep.kyri this turn's own record
